<title>BELGIUM: EU opens dumping probe into U.S. polymers.</title>
<headline>EU opens dumping probe into U.S. polymers.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it was opening an anti-dumping investigation into U.S. exports of polysulphide polymers.</p>
<p>It said it was responding to a complaint from AKCROS Chemicals GmbH &amp; Co KG., which charged that the volume and prices of the exports had harmed the European Union's industry.</p>
<p>The Commission said in the EU's Official Journal that there was sufficient evidence to justify a probe and gave interested parties 40 days to submit comments.</p>
</text>
